{"slug": "huevos-enfrijolados-eggs-in-spicy-black-beans", "nyt_id": 1026663, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1026663-huevos-enfrijolados-eggs-in-spicy-black-beans", "name": "Huevos Enfrijolados (Eggs in Spicy Black Beans)", "author": "Rick A. Martínez", "description": "Eggs nestled in a spicy, smoky black bean sauce, huevos enfrijolados are a staple of Mexican home cooking. It’s a quick way to make a meal from what’s already in the kitchen: leftover frijoles de olla, chiles and fresh eggs. In this version, canned black beans are cooked with chipotles and garlic until rich and creamy, then eggs are gently dropped into the simmering beans to poach. Served with crunchy tostadas, queso fresco and avocado, it’s a deeply comforting, pantry-friendly meal that comes together in under 45 minutes — perfect for a weeknight dinner or a quick and hearty brunch.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 5, "cook_minutes": 35, "total_minutes": 40, "raw": {"prep": "PT5M", "cook": "PT35M", "total": "PT40M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 tablespoons vegetable oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "vegetable oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ medium white onion, chopped (about ½ cup)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": null, "item": "medium white onion", "preparation": "chopped (about ½ cup)", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "3 garlic cloves, crushed", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "crushed", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "3 to 5 canned chipotle chiles in adobo (to taste), chopped, plus 2 tablespoons adobo sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "canned chipotle chiles in adobo", "preparation": "chopped, plus 2 tablespoons adobo sauce", "optional": false, "quantity_max": 5.0}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 (15-ounce) cans black beans, rinsed and drained", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "can", "item": "black beans", "preparation": "rinsed and drained", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 ¼ cups vegetable or mushroom broth", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "vegetable or mushroom broth", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Kosher salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "6 to 8 large eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": null, "item": "large eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false, "quantity_max": 8.0}, {"position": 9, "raw": "3 ounces queso fresco or Cotija cheese, crumbled", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "queso fresco or cotija cheese", "preparation": "crumbled", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Cilantro leaves with tender stems and sliced avocado, for serving", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "cilantro leaves with tender stems and sliced avocado", "preparation": "for serving", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "8 corn tostadas", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "unit": null, "item": "corn tostadas", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat oil in a large skillet over medium and add half of the onion, all of the garlic and the chopped chipotles, and cook, stirring occasionally, until tender and beginning to brown, 6 to 8 minutes. Add the beans, adobo sauce and broth and bring to a boil. Cook, stirring occasionally, until liquid has reduced slightly, about 5 minutes. Off the heat, use a potato masher to smash beans until no whole beans remain. Taste and season with salt."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Return the pan to medium-high.Use a spoon to make wells in the beans, gently crack the eggs into the simmering bean mixture and season each with salt. Reduce heat to medium and cook until the eggs are just set, 5 to 7 minutes. If you prefer hard-cooked eggs, cover the skillet and cook for 8 to 10 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Serve huevos enfrijolados with the queso, cilantro and remaining chopped onion sprinkled over the top, with sliced avocado and tostadas alongside."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 1028.75, "protein_g": 49.0, "carbohydrates_g": 100.4, "fat_g": 51.8, "saturated_fat_g": 18.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 6.4, "trans_fat_g": 0.3, "cholesterol_mg": 400.7, "sodium_mg": 2533.9, "fiber_g": 19.5, "sugar_g": 5.0, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mexican"], "diet": [], "course": ["breakfast-brunch-dinner-egg-dish-lunch-main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["black-bean", "chipotles-in-adobo", "easy", "egg", "one-pot", "quick", "skillet", "stovetop", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2025/03/28/multimedia/RM-huevos-enfrijoladas-vckf/RM-huevos-enfrijoladas-vckf-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2025/03/28/multimedia/RM-huevos-enfrijoladas-vckf/RM-huevos-enfrijoladas-vckf-googleFourByThree.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2025/03/28/multimedia/RM-huevos-enfrijoladas-vckf/RM-huevos-enfrijoladas-vckf-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2025/03/28/multimedia/RM-huevos-enfrijoladas-vckf/RM-huevos-enfrijoladas-vckf-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 1646}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2025-03-28", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:08:54Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "hummus-with-crisp-maitake-mushrooms", "nyt_id": 1013874, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013874-hummus-with-crisp-maitake-mushrooms", "name": "Hummus With Crisp Maitake Mushrooms", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "6 to 8 servings", "min": 6, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "PT20M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "Juice of 1 lemon, more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "juice of 1 lemon", "preparation": "more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 teaspoon kosher salt, more as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": "more as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ teaspoon ground cumin", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cumin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "½ teaspoon black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 fat garlic clove or 2 smaller cloves, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "fat garlic clove or 2 smaller cloves", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Pinch cayenne pepper, more for serving if desired", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "pinch cayenne pepper", "preparation": "more for serving if desired", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Pinch ground coriander", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "pinch ground coriander", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "⅓ cup tahini", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "unit": "cup", "item": "tahini", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "3 cups cooked chickpeas, or drained, canned chickpeas, warm or at room temperature", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "cooked chickpeas", "preparation": "or drained, canned chickpeas, warm or at room temperature", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¾ cup extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "3 ½ ounces maitake (hen-of-the-woods) or oyster mushrooms, cut into bite-size pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 3.5, "unit": "oz", "item": "maitake or oyster mushrooms", "preparation": "cut into bite-size pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "Chopped parsley", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "chopped parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "Sesame flatbread (see recipe) or raw vegetables or both", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "sesame flatbread or raw vegetables or both", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a food processor, combine the lemon juice, 1 teaspoon salt, cumin, black pepper, garlic, cayenne and coriander. Pulse the mixture just enough to blend."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Add tahini and ⅓ cup warm water. Pulse until smooth. Add the chickpeas and purée until smooth and creamy. This might take several minutes. With the motor running, drizzle in ½ cup oil. Taste and add more salt or lemon as needed."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Heat 3 tablespoons oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add the mushrooms. Cook, tossing occasionally, but not too often, so that the surface of the mushrooms have time to brown; cook until very crisp and dark golden, 7 to 10 minutes. Transfer to a paper-towel-lined dish to drain; sprinkle generously with salt while still hot."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Spread the hummus onto a platter and sprinkle with crisp mushrooms, parsley, cayenne if desired, and a drizzle of olive oil. Serve with flatbread or vegetables or both."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 355.125, "protein_g": 8.0, "carbohydrates_g": 21.4, "fat_g": 27.9, "saturated_fat_g": 3.8, "unsaturated_fat_g": 5.5, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 273.7, "fiber_g": 6.4, "sugar_g": 3.4, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer-hummus"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["chickpea", "fall", "quick", "tahini"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 37}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2011-10-19", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:47:02Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "hungarian-lentil-stew", "nyt_id": 1012675, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1012675-hungarian-lentil-stew", "name": "Hungarian Lentil Stew", "author": "Leslie Kaufman", "description": "Leslie Kaufman", "servings": {"text": "6 to 8 servings", "min": 6, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "PT1H"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 1-pound bag brown lentils", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "pound bag brown lentils", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons vegetable oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "vegetable oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 medium onion, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "medium onion", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "6 cloves garlic, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 tablespoons sweet Hungarian paprika", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sweet hungarian paprika", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "3 bay leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "bay leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 cups whole-fat sour cream", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "whole-fat sour cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "3 ½ tablespoons all-purpose flour", "group": null, "quantity": 3.5, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "all-purpose flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons milk", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "milk", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "½ teaspoon salt, or as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": "or as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 tablespoon light brown sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "light brown sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "2 tablespoons brown mustard, or as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "brown mustard", "preparation": "or as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "2 tablespoons fresh lemon juice, or as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": "or as needed", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "If desired, place lentils in a bowl with water to cover, and soak overnight; this step may be skipped, but makes lentils more digestible."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Place a large (5- to 6-quart) saucepan over medium-low heat, and add oil and onion. Sauté until tender, 1 to 2 minutes. Add garlic and paprika, and sauté until garlic is fragrant, 1 minute more. Add lentils, 8 cups water and bay leaves. Increase heat to bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low. Cover and simmer, stirring occasionally, until lentils are tender, about 50 minutes; add water as needed if mixture seems too thick."}, {"position": 3, "text": "When lentils are tender, in a small bowl stir together sour cream, flour and milk. Add to lentils and simmer 2 to 3 minutes. Add salt, brown sugar, mustard and lemon juice, adjusting amounts as needed for a slightly piquant flavor. If desired, remove and discard bay leaves. Serve hot."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 373.125, "protein_g": 16.5, "carbohydrates_g": 46.1, "fat_g": 14.9, "saturated_fat_g": 6.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 1.4, "trans_fat_g": 0.5, "cholesterol_mg": 34.3, "sodium_mg": 213.7, "fiber_g": 7.3, "sugar_g": 5.3, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["eastern-european"], "diet": []